            "publicNotes": "<p>Though always dressed like they're attending the finest court functions, a kaztili behaves more like the patron of an ale hall. Consummate comedians and witty debaters, these liminal sprites love ambages and flyting. Though to outsiders, their interests might seem align with those of murxies, most kaztilis look down on such fellows, considering them low-brow hacks, though others cultivate eager followings of the weaker fey. Kaztilis appear as miniature elves, but with angular, gossamer wings sprouting from their backs.</p><hr /><p>Elusive, flighty, and ebullient, sprites are what many villagers first imagine when they hear the terms \"fey\" or \"fairy.\"</p>",
            "publication": {
                "license": "ORC",
                "remaster": true,
                "title": "Pathfinder Feybound"
            }
